```

The problem seems to be that it's written to expect a trailing or leading `&`, i.e. that example would work if it was:

```js
    axios('/foo', {
      baseURL: 'http://a.com?b=c&',
                             // ^
      params: {
        a: 42
      }
    });
```

but that seems like a really awkward thing to expect people to write (and leaves the trailing `&` in the case where you don't add any non-default query params). I don't think this is the right approach to default params; I suggested alternatives [here][1].

